// Define the Cache interface
public interface Cache<K, V> {
    void put(K key, V value);
    V get(K key);
    void remove(K key);
}

// Implement a simple in-memory cache with LRU eviction policy
public class LRUCache<K, V> implements Cache<K, V> {
    private final int capacity;
    private final Map<K, V> cache;

    public LRUCache(int capacity) {
        this.capacity = capacity;
        this.cache = new LinkedHashMap<>(capacity, 0.75f, true) {
            protected boolean removeEldestEntry(Map.Entry eldest) {
                return size() > LRUCache.this.capacity;
            }
        };
    }

    @Override
    public void put(K key, V value) {
        cache.put(key, value);
    }

    @Override
    public V get(K key) {
        return cache.getOrDefault(key, null);
    }

    @Override
    public void remove(K key) {
        cache.remove(key);
    }
}

// Define a DataProcessor interface
public interface DataProcessor {
    void process(String data);
}

// Implement a data processor that uses the cache
public class CachedDataProcessor implements DataProcessor {
    private final Cache<String, String> cache;

    public CachedDataProcessor(Cache<String, String> cache) {
        this.cache = cache;
    }

    @Override
    public void process(String data) {
        if (cache.get(data) != null) {
            System.out.println("Cache hit: " + data);
        } else {
            System.out.println("Processing new data: " + data);
            // Simulate data processing
            try {
                Thread.sleep(100);
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
            }
            cache.put(data, data.toUpperCase());
        }
    }
}

// Main class to demonstrate the framework
public class CachingFrameworkExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Cache<String, String> cache = new LRUCache<>(10);
        DataProcessor processor = new CachedDataProcessor(cache);

        // Simulate real-time data processing
        for (int i = 0; i < 20; i++) {
            processor.process("data" + i % 5);
        }
    }
}
```

This code provides a basic implementation of a caching and data processing framework in Java. It includes an in-memory cache with an LRU eviction policy, a data processor that uses the cache to avoid redundant processing of data, and a simple demonstration of how these components can be integrated.']

